    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d302">

                <pb facs="0471" n="391" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg391"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">762.94/76: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dickover</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-11-11T18:00:00+09:00">November 11,
                            1936—6 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 11—7:11 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>231. Twice recently vernacular newspapers have published guarded references to an
                    unspecified but allegedly important diplomatic project under consideration by
                    the Government, the <hi rendition="#italic">Asahi</hi> this morning stating that
                    the matter will be submitted to the Privy Council for approval. The submission
                    of the matter to the Privy Council suggests that an agreement which requires
                    Imperial sanction is under consideration, and credence is given in well-informed
                    circles in Tokyo to a report that the diplomatic project in question has to do
                    with Germany and that it is being opposed by the liberal group in the
                    Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dickover</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
